Day 20 - pip & Virtual Environment (venv)

Topics Covered

- Introduction to "pip"
- Installing Python packages
- Common pip commands ("install", "list", "show", "uninstall")
- Virtual Environment ("venv")
- Creating and activating a virtual environment
- "requirements.txt" and "pip freeze"

Key Learnings

- "pip" is Python's package manager used to install external libraries.
- A virtual environment creates an isolated Python environment for each project.
- "requirements.txt" stores the list of project dependencies, making it easy to recreate the same environment on another system.

